1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,513
This is ATLAS, a financial research workspace for Indian and global markets.

2
00:00:05,513 --> 00:00:11,220
Everything you will see is the local build running on this computer, using real data

3
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,510
from named sources.

4
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:15,500
The narration is a synthetic computer voice.

5
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,762
ATLAS opens on a globe built from real geography.

6
00:00:20,762 --> 00:00:24,384
Gold points are places and markets with stored data.

7
00:00:24,384 --> 00:00:30,234
Enter ATLAS leads straight into your workspace; returning visitors skip this screen.

8
00:00:38,034 --> 00:00:40,416
Home is a personal command centre.

9
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:44,619
One next step leads, chosen from what you said you came for.

10
00:00:44,619 --> 00:00:50,573
Below it are today’s research mission, saved research with its real figures, research

11
00:00:50,573 --> 00:00:53,514
updates and the pages you opened recently.

12
00:00:53,514 --> 00:00:59,468
In Explore mode, the ATLAS Universe is one click away; Focus mode keeps the same page

13
00:00:59,468 --> 00:01:00,589
quiet and dense.

14
00:01:15,491 --> 00:01:21,201
Further down are end-of-day Indian indices from EODHD, commodity benchmarks, macro

15
00:01:21,201 --> 00:01:25,517
indicators from FRED, and reference prices for digital assets.

16
00:01:25,517 --> 00:01:31,366
Status tags say whether each series is as recent as its publication schedule allows.

17
00:01:32,617 --> 00:01:34,834
Search is one keystroke away.

18
00:01:34,834 --> 00:01:41,409
Control K opens the command palette, and plain words work: rupee finds the rupee to US

19
00:01:41,409 --> 00:01:43,014
dollar exchange rate.

20
00:01:43,014 --> 00:01:49,742
Search covers indices, macro series, commodities, Academy lessons and your own research.

21
00:01:49,742 --> 00:01:53,182
When something is not available, it says why.

22
00:01:54,435 --> 00:01:58,831
The ATLAS Universe turns the same idea into a place to explore.

23
00:01:58,831 --> 00:02:04,762
Select India and the panel lists what is stored: the three indices at end of day, the

24
00:02:04,762 --> 00:02:08,042
rupee and Indian inflation, each with its date.

25
00:02:08,042 --> 00:02:13,904
It also says what is not available, such as individual shares, which need a licence.

26
00:02:15,155 --> 00:02:19,583
The Intelligence Network shows how stored series moved together.

27
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:25,535
Each line is a measured correlation of weekly changes: gold moved together, blue moved

28
00:02:25,535 --> 00:02:26,158
opposite.

29
00:02:26,158 --> 00:02:31,832
Select Brent crude and the panel ranks its relationships, with the number of weeks

30
00:02:31,832 --> 00:02:32,940
behind each one.

31
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:36,469
Correlation is not causation, and the page says so.

32
00:02:39,823 --> 00:02:45,457
Market Pulse shows what moved and what was published, grouped by how current it is.

33
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:50,955
In the move field, each column of particles is one instrument, sized by its move.

34
00:02:50,955 --> 00:02:56,454
Further down, the largest moves and record highs and lows are found in the stored

35
00:02:56,454 --> 00:02:57,472
history itself.

36
00:03:10,778 --> 00:03:17,210
A macro series page shows the latest value, the period it refers to, when FRED first

37
00:03:17,210 --> 00:03:20,425
published it, and when ATLAS retrieved it.

38
00:03:20,425 --> 00:03:26,933
The chart has range presets, a hover read-out, drag to zoom, CSV export, a table view

39
00:03:26,933 --> 00:03:28,158
and full screen.

40
00:03:35,448 --> 00:03:41,046
Commodities covers global benchmarks such as Brent and WTI crude, natural gas and

41
00:03:41,046 --> 00:03:45,954
metals, with US inventories from the Energy Information Administration.

42
00:03:45,954 --> 00:03:51,968
Indian futures are not shown, because exchange terms do not permit automated collection

43
00:03:51,968 --> 00:03:53,212
without a licence.

44
00:03:54,468 --> 00:03:59,455
Indian markets covers the indices that the free EODHD plan provides.

45
00:03:59,455 --> 00:04:03,708
Closes are end of day, and final after the evening update.

46
00:04:03,708 --> 00:04:05,762
ATLAS never calls them live.

47
00:04:07,024 --> 00:04:12,526
Digital assets uses CoinGecko reference prices, requested at a pace that stays within

48
00:04:12,526 --> 00:04:14,274
the free monthly allowance.

49
00:04:16,347 --> 00:04:20,275
The research hub brings the analysis tools together.

50
00:04:20,275 --> 00:04:26,393
A research portfolio is hypothetical: ATLAS holds no assets and places no orders.

51
00:04:26,393 --> 00:04:29,489
This one holds bitcoin, ether and solana.

52
00:04:29,489 --> 00:04:36,060
ATLAS reports total return, maximum drawdown, volatility, contribution by holding and a

53
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:42,707
stress scenario, and lists the source, venue and coverage of every price series it used.

54
00:04:43,959 --> 00:04:47,036
Quantitative research is tested out of sample.

55
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:52,922
The walk-forward backtest chooses a moving-average rule on each training window and then

56
00:04:52,922 --> 00:04:57,805
measures it only on the following, unseen window, with fees and slippage.

57
00:04:57,805 --> 00:05:03,022
Here, on bitcoin since 2015, the rule earned less than simply holding, and the

58
00:05:03,022 --> 00:05:07,369
training-window return is labelled as optimistic by construction.

59
00:05:08,625 --> 00:05:14,461
The notebook keeps notes, hypotheses and reflections, each with its assumptions and

60
00:05:14,461 --> 00:05:17,415
counterarguments, and exports to Markdown.

61
00:05:17,415 --> 00:05:22,970
Reports turn a research question and a set of instruments into a dated, sourced

62
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:23,603
document.

63
00:05:23,603 --> 00:05:25,924
Both are private to your account.

64
00:05:27,175 --> 00:05:29,564
The Academy teaches with evidence.

65
00:05:29,564 --> 00:05:32,164
Courses begin with a readiness check.

66
00:05:32,164 --> 00:05:37,716
Progress earns XP, levels and achievements for real work: lessons, quizzes, and

67
00:05:37,716 --> 00:05:42,214
documented research such as a correlation study in the explorer.

68
00:05:43,465 --> 00:05:46,804
The Academy can be explored as a constellation.

69
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:52,913
Each course is a cluster and each lesson a star; gold stars are lessons completed, and

70
00:05:52,913 --> 00:05:55,257
the pulsing star is the next one.

71
00:05:55,257 --> 00:05:57,530
It shows recorded progress only.

72
00:06:01,972 --> 00:06:07,197
Every course opens with a narrated introduction video, with English captions and a

73
00:06:07,197 --> 00:06:09,426
transcript; the voice is synthetic.

74
00:06:09,426 --> 00:06:14,969
Lessons then move through stages, from discovery and prediction to a worked example and

75
00:06:14,969 --> 00:06:18,282
a short quiz, and progress is saved to your account.

76
00:06:19,548 --> 00:06:25,422
Data sources shows where each dataset comes from, how current it is, and the state of

77
00:06:25,422 --> 00:06:27,219
every provider connection.

78
00:06:27,219 --> 00:06:29,983
Rate limits are respected automatically.

79
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:34,614
The same workspace adapts to a phone screen.

80
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,317
Some limits are worth stating plainly.

81
00:06:45,317 --> 00:06:51,483
There are no individual Indian shares or company financials yet, because no licensed

82
00:06:51,483 --> 00:06:52,952
source is connected.

83
00:06:52,952 --> 00:06:56,329
Gold and silver have no permitted free source.

84
00:06:56,329 --> 00:06:58,384
End-of-day data is not live.

85
00:06:58,384 --> 00:07:02,862
ATLAS is a research and learning tool, not investment advice.
